<overview>
<p>Caesar's ongoing program to modernize the Legiones Marianes has extended to conventional infantry formations, with improved equipment and weapons gradually replacing older stockpiles across the Hegemony's auxiliary legions. A contubernium is the smallest tactical unit in the Marian system, equivalent to a single reinforced squad of ten soldiers. Foot contubernia serve as sentries, checkpoint garrisons, and building-clearing teams in urban operations where larger formations cannot maneuver effectively. Command personnel carry sidearms and rifles suited to personal defense rather than front-line engagement, reflecting their primary role as coordinators rather than riflemen.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Marian Hegemony infantry platoons consist of a 100-trooper Century comprised of ten 10-trooper contubernia or squads. Game play requires this to be broken down into units of 30 or fewer troopers, with the Duplus Contubernium being a two-squad (20 trooper) deployment and the Triplus Contubernium being a three-squad (30 trooper) deployment.
</notes>

